WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.457 --> 00:00:15.218
my hat?"

2
00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:16.438
Nan shouted.

3
00:00:16.458 --> 00:00:20.620
"Mrs. Bauer says I can't leave without my hat!"

4
00:00:24.882 --> 00:00:26.562
"Has anybody seen my pail?"

5
00:00:26.942 --> 00:00:27.783
Tommy asked.

6
00:00:27.803 --> 00:00:30.244
"It was here a minute ago."

7
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:36.624
The children were getting ready to pick huckleberries on an August afternoon.

8
00:00:37.785 --> 00:00:42.149
The floor of the hallway was covered with hats, pails, and snacks.

9
00:00:42.169 --> 00:00:45.492
"I can't wait to pick huckleberries!"

10
00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:48.395
Rob announced happily as he joined the group.

11
00:00:50.997 --> 00:00:53.860
Jo sighed when she saw her five-year-old son.

12
00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:58.444
"It's much too far for you to walk, Rob.

13
00:00:59.628 --> 00:01:03.089
You'll get so hot and tired that you won't have a good time."

14
00:01:03.109 --> 00:01:07.510
"We're going all the way to the big pasture.

15
00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:10.371
We don't want you tagging along," Jack said.

16
00:01:10.391 --> 00:01:12.551
"I can keep up!"

17
00:01:12.792 --> 00:01:13.732
Rob insisted.

18
00:01:13.752 --> 00:01:19.573
"Oh, Mama, let me go—I want to fill my new pail with berries for you."

19
00:01:19.593 --> 00:01:29.176
"If you wait until I can take you," Jo replied, "we'll pick as many berries as you want."

20
00:01:31.112 --> 00:01:37.337
"You're always too busy to go," Rob said, starting to sob.

21
00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:46.245
The sight of Rob's tears touched everyone but Jack, who thought Rob was a nuisance.

22
00:01:46.265 --> 00:01:52.530
"I'll stay home with him," Daisy offered, putting down her pail.

23
00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:56.434
"Oh, let him come," Nan said.

24
00:01:56.454 --> 00:01:58.876
"I'll take good care of him."

25
00:02:01.276 --> 00:02:05.539
"I'd carry him if I could," Dan murmured, looking down at his foot.

26
00:02:05.559 --> 00:02:11.102
"But I guess I can't go, even though I'm not using a crutch anymore."

27
00:02:11.122 --> 00:02:18.366
"Thank you for offering, Dan," Jo said, "but you shouldn't overdo things.

28
00:02:20.307 --> 00:02:22.148
Wait a minute, I have an idea."

29
00:02:23.489 --> 00:02:24.750
She raced outside.

30
00:02:26.591 --> 00:02:31.218
Silas was driving away in the cart but turned back when he noticed Jo.

31
00:02:33.559 --> 00:02:37.142
A few minutes later she returned to the house, beaming.

32
00:02:37.162 --> 00:02:44.006
"I've arranged things so everyone—including Rob and Dan—can go," Jo explained.

33
00:02:44.026 --> 00:02:49.410
"Silas will drive you to the pasture, and pick you up at five o'clock."

34
00:02:50.731 --> 00:02:52.492
"Hooray!" Rob shouted.

35
00:02:52.512 --> 00:02:57.196
"I won't eat a single berry, Mama—I'll save them all for you!"

36
00:02:58.992 --> 00:03:02.874
Everyone had a delightful afternoon despite some mishaps.

37
00:03:08.657 --> 00:03:14.120
Tommy was stung by a wasp, and Jack fell out of a tree.

38
00:03:17.841 --> 00:03:22.944
Startled by a snake, Daisy dropped her pail and spilled half her berries.

39
00:03:25.036 --> 00:03:29.940
But the boys weren't badly hurt, and Demi helped Daisy refill her pail.

40
00:03:31.682 --> 00:03:37.706
Meanwhile Dan enjoyed himself, observing wild creatures in the grass and sky.

41
00:03:39.168 --> 00:03:43.231
While the others stayed together, Nan wandered off with Rob.

42
00:03:43.251 --> 00:03:49.556
"I keep putting berries in my pail, but it doesn't fill up," Rob complained.

43
00:03:51.117 --> 00:03:54.080
Nan pointed to the woods beyond a stone wall.

44
00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:59.221
"Last time the bushes over there had much bigger berries," she said.

45
00:03:59.241 --> 00:04:03.622
"We discovered a cave, and the boys built a fire.

46
00:04:05.543 --> 00:04:09.804
If we went there, we could fill our pails and hide in the cave till everyone found us."

47
00:04:12.965 --> 00:04:17.086
They scrambled over the wall and ran through a field to the woods.

48
00:04:17.106 --> 00:04:24.160
"These bushes do have the best huckleberries!"

49
00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:25.881
Rob said as they filled their pails.

50
00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:29.643
"Now we'll find the cave and have something to eat."

51
00:04:29.663 --> 00:04:33.105
"Are you sure you know the way?"

52
00:04:33.485 --> 00:04:34.206
Rob asked.

53
00:04:34.226 --> 00:04:36.227
"Of course!"

54
00:04:36.827 --> 00:04:39.569
Nan replied, sounding very certain.

55
00:04:39.589 --> 00:04:45.652
"I have an excellent sense of direction—remember when I fetched my suitcase all by myself?"

56
00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:54.584
That convinced Rob, and he followed Nan, who after much meandering, finally located the cave.

57
00:04:57.185 --> 00:04:59.646
They crawled inside to wait for the others.

58
00:04:59.666 --> 00:05:02.187
"Isn't this nice?"

59
00:05:02.607 --> 00:05:05.248
Nan said, offering some bread to Rob.

60
00:05:05.268 --> 00:05:09.909
"Yes, but do you think they'll find us soon?"

61
00:05:11.149 --> 00:05:13.290
Rob was getting bored and restless.

62
00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:20.232
"No, because when we hear them, we'll stay quiet, and then we'll have fun watching them search for

63
00:05:20.392 --> 00:05:23.585
us!" "What if they don't come?"

64
00:05:24.005 --> 00:05:24.746
Rob asked.

65
00:05:24.766 --> 00:05:29.248
"I can find the way home by myself even though it's six miles."

66
00:05:31.129 --> 00:05:35.232
Nan had only a vague idea of distance but a lot of confidence.

67
00:05:37.053 --> 00:05:40.915
After a while Rob said, "I guess we should go now."

68
00:05:42.256 --> 00:05:45.478
"Not until I sort through my berries," Nan said.

69
00:05:46.699 --> 00:05:52.578
Rob tried to wait patiently while Nan slowly examined every berry for flaws.

70
00:05:52.598 --> 00:05:55.139
"Oh no!"

71
00:05:55.499 --> 00:05:58.180
he said as the sun dropped behind a hill.

72
00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:02.802
"You said you'd take good care of me, and it's getting dark."

73
00:06:02.822 --> 00:06:08.504
"What?" Startled, Nan looked up from her work.

74
00:06:08.524 --> 00:06:11.646
"We have to get going before they leave without us."

75
00:06:11.666 --> 00:06:20.654
"I heard somebody blowing a horn an hour ago," Rob said, but unfortunately his sense of time was

76
00:06:20.734 --> 00:06:22.775
no better than Nan's sense of distance.

77
00:06:22.795 --> 00:06:26.876
"Maybe everybody was searching for us."

78
00:06:28.417 --> 00:06:30.538
"Which direction did the sound come from?"

79
00:06:30.938 --> 00:06:31.659
Nan asked.

80
00:06:31.679 --> 00:06:36.681
"Um Rob said, hesitating before he pointed.

81
00:06:36.701 --> 00:06:38.382
"Over there?"

82
00:06:39.922 --> 00:06:43.404
Nan took off, while Rob tried his best to keep up.

83
00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:49.322
They climbed up and down hills, pausing to listen for the horn.

84
00:06:51.123 --> 00:06:55.566
But they never heard it because it had only been the sound of a cow mooing.

85
00:06:55.586 --> 00:07:02.810
"I don't remember seeing that pile of stones," Nan said as they rested on a wall.

86
00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:07.752
Suddenly her face brightened, and she pointed to something.

87
00:07:07.772 --> 00:07:11.094
"Look—there's the tree that Jack fell from."

88
00:07:12.775 --> 00:07:16.582
But when they reached the tree, it was not the one Jack had climbed.

89
00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:20.585
"Are we lost?"

90
00:07:20.945 --> 00:07:22.486
Rob's voice trembled.

91
00:07:22.506 --> 00:07:28.110
"Not really—I just don't see which way to go right now.

92
00:07:29.271 --> 00:07:39.759
If we shout, I'm sure they'll hear The two children shouted until they were hoarse, but no one

93
00:07:40.019 --> 00:07:45.971
answered. "I wish Mama would come find us," Rob said.

94
00:07:45.991 --> 00:07:48.814
"Oh, look, there she is!"

95
00:07:50.175 --> 00:07:54.379
Rob ran toward a dim figure slowly approaching them in the dark.

96
00:07:55.720 --> 00:08:00.224
Suddenly he stopped, turned around, and came stumbling back to Nan.

97
00:08:00.244 --> 00:08:05.749
"That's not Mama," he screamed.

98
00:08:05.769 --> 00:08:07.951
"It's a bear!"
